# MetaEuk's own output, and the two files this pipeline derives from it, are not
# byte-stable across machines: MetaEuk is MMseqs2-derived and orders its results by
# how the work was distributed, so the same input gives the same content in a
# different order elsewhere. Confirmed on CI, where one job produced different md5s
# for these six files while the identical shard on the other Nextflow version matched
# -- and where multiqc_metaeuk_stats.txt, derived from them, stayed byte-identical.
# Their presence is still asserted through stable_name, the ORF count and mean length
# through the MultiQC stats file, and the FASTA/GFF id contract through the explicit
# assertions in tests/metaeuk.nf.test.
metaeuk/*.fas
metaeuk/*.gff
metaeuk/*.headersMap.tsv
metaeuk/*_format.faa.gz
metaeuk/*_format.gff.gz
# QUAST's quast.log and report.html/report.tex embed run timestamps and
# work-directory-specific absolute paths, so only file presence (stable_path), not
# content, is asserted. MultiQC's own parsed quast tables are ignored too: MEGAHIT has
# no fixed seed (see the MEGAHIT non-determinism note this repo already carries for
# assembly-derived checksums), so N50/L50/largest-contig/GC%/etc. can shift slightly
# between runs even though contig *count* usually doesn't -- confirmed flaky in CI on
# quast_table.txt for both 'test' and 'test_kofamscan'.
quast/**
multiqc/multiqc_data/multiqc_quast.txt
multiqc/multiqc_data/quast_table.txt
multiqc/multiqc_data/quast_num_contigs.txt
trimgalore/fastqc/*.{html,zip}
trimgalore/*trimming_report.txt
pipeline_info/nf_core_metatdenovo_software_mqc_versions.yml
samtools/*.flagstat
samtools/*.idxstats
samtools/*.stats
trimgalore/fastqc/*_fastqc.{html,zip}
multiqc/multiqc_data/bbduk*.txt
multiqc/multiqc_data/bbduk-filtered*.txt
